# 22 — Close the core program with an evidence-backed decision

**Goal / what to deliver:** Deliver a reproducible account of which representations help perception and forecasting, with explicit adoption/rejection decisions.

**Blocked by:** [12](12-swformer-comparison.md), [13](13-rsn-range-study.md), [16](16-r4d-distance.md), [18](18-mask-to-lidar.md), [21](21-forecast-feature-study.md)

**Status:** planned — blocked by prerequisite verification

**Lane:** core

**Verifier:** Independent audit from preregistration to raw exports, metric summaries, receipts and conclusions; replay one selected held-out comparison from each primary study in live Insula.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every required core ticket has its own validated candidate-specific live receipt and scientific report where applicable.
- [ ] Publish controlled results, uncertainty, coverage, resource costs, limitations and negative findings; no cherry-picked successful scenes.
- [ ] Choose adopt/reject/needs-more-evidence for mask transfer and sensor-feature forecasting according to frozen rules.
- [ ] Planning/safety claims and unverified cross-dataset correspondences are excluded; follow-on tickets activate only with their evidence gates.
- [ ] Independently validate live Insula receipt, candidate/input/runtime identities, required assertions, output hashes and measured resources; missing or failed checks prohibit closure.
- [ ] Publish a reviewable evidence summary with exact replay recipe, observed outcome and limitations; existing host tests or historical receipts alone do not close this ticket.

## Binding completion policy

[Program goal and evidence policy](program-goal.md) applies in full. Preparation may occur before blockers clear; candidate execution/promotion and completion require verified blockers. Scientific completion permits negative/inconclusive findings. Adoption requires the separately stated promotion rule.
